run dir fresh + the per-run lock `mkdir <run dir>/.exp38_lock`. Before the fork: at-launch record + the **immutable tool snapshot** `<run dir>/.exp38_tools/` = every file of the closure digest + the subset-audit artifact + E0/SMOKE receipts, `SNAPSHOT.sha256`; the start watcher, end gate and audits execute the snapshot (`python <snap>/…/exp38_registry.py --repo <snap> …`). Launch `setsid python train.py …` → log; start watcher (log gate + evidence gate; on failure terminates ONLY our process group); end gate; cadence set; B2 audit; `CHECKPOINTS.sha256`; lock released. **SMOKE_DDP receipt schema** (`data_efficiency_smoke_<run>_<ts>.json` + `.sha256`, smoke dir under `outputs_FLAC/exp38_smoke/`, never the NAS run namespace): run, platform, closure digest, environment-receipt sha, production-relevant argv projection (the FULL argv minus max-steps / checkpoint-every / save-dir / names), arm / dataset / split shas, backend probe, the B3 evidence summary of both ranks, GPU names + UUIDs, DDP members 1/2 + 2/2, ≥ 1 optimizer step, finite losses, zero checkpoints, exit statuses, verdict. Guard tests (`test_exp38_launchers.py`) drive the real script in DRY_RUN with synthetic environments (fake `nvidia-smi` on PATH, temp roots via DRY_RUN-only hooks) for every refusal.
