   179	## 11. Validation ladder
   180	
   181	1. Static (`py_compile`, `bash -n`, `json.load`, `git diff --check`). 2. pytest: all new tests + the existing suites on the touched / used code. 3. Subset audit + `--verify` on the real tree. 4. CPU: init digest, B4a on the real DINOv3 weights. 5. DRY_RUN of every launch path (registry `dry-run` both platforms, `MODE=DRY_RUN` per run, `DRY_RUN=1` submitter and `EXP38_SBATCH_DRYRUN=1` per run, `exp38_eval.py plan`). 6. GPU-0 single-rank smoke now (≤ 15 min total, Yixun-allowed; YAW f025 and B-F f025, 20 steps, micro 32, no checkpoint; evidence callback on): banner, finite loss, flash counted, B-F call shapes, peak memory (B-F ≈ 15–16 GiB/rank expected), single-rank rate (lower bound only; promotes nothing). 7. At campaign start, on idle cards: environment receipt → E0 (8 cells) → SMOKE_DDP per run → FULL. 8. Nothing beyond rung 6 is run by the Coder.
   182	
   183	## 12. Launch acceptance criteria (per run)
   184	
   185	All §10 B6 gates pass; the start watcher sees DDP members 1/2 + 2/2, the dataset line (count / 243) on both ranks, the YAW banner before step 0 (YAW), finite losses, and the B3 evidence of both ranks satisfying every listed condition; checkpoints exactly every 2,500 steps; the end gate (Lightning's `max_steps=40000` marker, ≥ 50 finite parsed losses, none non-finite); the step-40000 B2 audit; `CHECKPOINTS.sha256`; exit statuses of train.py and the watcher recorded; never resumed.
   186	
   187	## 13. Decisions for Yixun (with recommendations)
   188	
   189	- **D1 rung:** 2 ranks × 32 everywhere (recommended); 8×8 only as a labelled cross-recipe run.
   190	- **D2 platform / allocation:** (a) **all six on this box, sequential, exclusive** (recommended; ≈ 11–13.3 days incl. E0, smokes and evals); (b) B-F × 3 here + YAW × 3 on neuronic 2×L40 with the mandatory P1 bridge — the YAW 25–75 % points share a platform but its 100 % anchor stays A6000-trained (Codex r2 NIT 3), so that curve is cross-platform at 100 %; (c) the brief's split — not recommended (the B-F curve mixes A6000 and L40 within 25–75 %), and if chosen the bridge is mandatory and every A6000/L40 comparison is labelled sensitivity.
   191	- **D3 crash policy:** fixed by §6 (re-run from 0; resumed = sensitivity only). No decision needed unless Yixun wants exact-resume machinery built.
   192	- **D4 training backend:** flash (recommended; = the documented P1 / B-F backend); SDPA would match dc_van's training. The evidence gate refuses a mismatch either way.
   193	- **D5 GPU policy here:** idle (recommended), sequenced by the main session through the `claude_gpu_yield` handshake.
   194	- **D6 E0a mismatch:** decided at that moment by Yixun (§9.3).
   195	- **D7 table regeneration:** neuronic regen after each results commit (recommended; repo practice) vs here with the row-regression overrides (needs his explicit order).
   196	
   197	## 14. Risks and disclosures
   198	
   199	One training seed per cell; matched steps, not epochs or compute. Historical asymmetries: dc_van trained SDPA (ours flash, D4); different code / dependency eras (§5); P1 100 % resumed at 32.5k; YAW 100 %'s launch source and training backend unknown; W&B vs `--logger none` (operational); any non-A6000 platform (D2). E0 removes evaluation-side doubt only. Concurrent writers: runs launch from the frozen campaign worktree; a closure change after a launch = a new run. Never edit a running bash script (bodies are single functions called on the last line); never touch another session's processes or the handshake files; the Coder starts no real training.
