   153	`exp38_collect.py` admits a cell as one transaction (Codex r1 HIGH 8, r2 HIGH 9): exact raw `metrics` key set, all finite; protocol fields (`cond_method`, `frame_avg_angles`, `frame_avg_fwd_cap`, `orbit_execution`, `cond_autocast bf16`, `rotate_deg 0`, `seed`, `steps 1`, `cfg_scale 1.0`, `batch_size 64`, `n_samples 6337`, `device cuda`, `dataset_config`, `eval_name`, `weights_source ema`, `source_sha`, `per_scene_schema 1`, `scene_count 10` and the ten expected scene keys); `ckpt_sha256_loaded` / `ckpt_bytes_loaded` = the run's admitted final checkpoint; stream sidecar (`stream_count 6337`, pinned `input_hash`); the driver's cell receipt (model / dataset config shas, `data/AR/unseen_eval.json` and AGREE checkpoint shas, launcher sentinel, rc 0, metrics + stream + dump paths and shas — the cross-links); dump `COMPLETE` + `manifest.json` + `waveforms.npy` `[6337, 10240]` float32 + sha; exactly seeds 42–46 per (run, K), no duplicates. Runs with a `RESUMED_AT_*` marker never enter the primary table. Results `data_efficiency_results.{json,md}` are written under a collector lock as one atomic pair (temp files → fsync → renames, JSON last-renamed-first-read with a manifest sha in the MD), with a campaign manifest of every admitted file. Incomplete → PENDING.
